The European Union and India will double vomit trade.
“Since the European Union and India are mutually leading trade partners, the agenda of the ninth summit has also been dominated, along with other major global problems.
Today there will also be a Franco-Indian summit, which will focus on cooperation in nuclear power.
The European Union acknowledges that India is an uplifting democratic super-power that should have a greater say in international affairs, but the member states have not yet managed to reach a common denominator to support New Delhi’s permanent membership in the United Nations Security Council.
This issue has not been challenged at the ninth summit held yesterday in Marseille.
French President Nicolas Sarkozy, the President-in-Office of the Council of the European Union and Commission President José Manuel Barroso and High Representative Javier Solana, received Indian Prime Minister Manmohan Singh, with whom they agreed to double in five years, i.e. increasing trade turnover to more than a hundred billion euros.
Considering that between 2000 and 2007 the exchange of commodities increased from EUR 25 billion to EUR 55 billion, this is not an overly ambitious target.
In doing so, the twenty-six bilateral civil aviation treaties with India have been consolidated in a legal sense, i.e. air traffic could soar in the future.
India intends to sign a free trade agreement with the EU by the end of 2009.
Sarkozy has pledged to accelerate negotiations.
The goal is to rebalancing that while the EU is India’s number one trading partner, New Delhi ranks only ninth among EU partners.
The summit paid its attention to global affairs.
The Afghan-Captan and Pakistani situation, as well as of terrorism, was condemned in all its forms on both sides and called for the convening of the United Nations convening.
They have also called for an end to the Doha trade round, although they both have a large part in the failure so far so far.
The EU has reaffirmed its insistence on its energy and climate programme, i.e. to reduce emissions by at least 20 per cent by 2020.
India has also agreed, as well as the need to make a global deal at next year’s climate conference and reduce the production of greenhouse gases by 50 percent by 2050.
I would also like to hamper the rise in food prices and supported the convening of an international meeting to review the financial crisis.
The Prime Minister of India is now going to the French capital, where at the bilateral meeting he intends to make a deal about the peaceful use of nuclear energy.
In Paris, it is hoped that the construction of Indian nuclear reactors will be commissioned by French companies worth 20 billion euros.
According to the news agency, the agreement would last for 15 years.
More than three hundred Italian publishers in Frankfurt
Italian publishers are strongly represented at the Frankfurt International Book Fair.
More than three-hundred Italian publishing houses will be present at the 60th Buchmesse fair.
7,000 exhibitors from 1,17,7,7,7,7,790 sqm are expected at this year’s Frankfurt International Book Fair.
At the opening ceremonies of the Italian pavilion, Francesco Maria Giro, Deputy Secretary of State of the Ministry of Culture and Activities, will occupy a 264-square-square-metre exhibition area through the establishment of a unified Italia.
The ceremonial reunion will be followed by a press conference to be held in the "Room Struktur" room of pavilion 5.0 Buchmesse, where there will also be an opportunity to present data, trends and prospects regarding the situation of Italian publishing.
According to the data, in the Italian publishing market the proportion of foreign authors is steadily declining, especially in the field of adult and youth publications.
Steve Fossett’s plane, a billion-finished billionaire, has been found a year ago.
They found the remnants of the billion-dollar Steve Fossett, who disappeared over the Nevada desert on September 3, 2007.
The wreckage was found on a 3,000-metre-tall plateau near Mammoth Lakes in the Sierra-Nidom mountains on the outskirts of California and Nevada.
There were no human remnants inside the plane.
John Anderson, the Sheriff of Madera County, disassociated any remaining doubts: “After determining the location of the plane, we sent out a team, and now we can be sure that it’s the plane that Steve Fossett flew on the day he disappeared,” he said at a press conference at a press conference.
The sheriff has also confirmed that no human remains have been found either in the plane or the surrounding area.
The 63-year-old was pronounced dead in February.
The U.S. Transportation Safety Administration (NTSB) has said a few hours after the discovery of the decompose, an investigative committee was asked to identify the plane and to determine whether it’s the Bellanca 8kcab, which disappeared on September 3, 2007, on the day when Fosett went on a three-hour flight from Yerington in Nevada.
Yesterday in California, not far from the limit of Nevada, a couple found some of Fossett’s personal belongings near his home in Mammoth Lakes.
Two Illections in the name of Fosset were issued by the Illinois Federal Aviation Administration, some cash and a sweater.
The search for Fossett was dispatched a month after his disappearance.
The billion-billionaire set a number of culminated in history.
On his sixth attempt in 2002, he was the first to fly around the earth with a balloon: two weeks of solitary flying.
Thirty-two years later, by plane, he orbited the earth without landing.
Many of his records include flying above the Andes at an altitude of 14,545 meters, with a co-pilot.
GLK, astonishing advertisement
An unfamiliar recreational SUV with its original and distinct design, with large surfaces and clean corners.
In a few words, this is Mercedes-Benz’s latest “compact off-road vehicle”, with which the German automaker was trying to bring fresh momentum to the market.
Due to this, the introductory campaign of the SUV GLK available in Mercedes-Benz showrooms from 17 October will be surprising and unconventional.
The advertising campaign accompanying the introduction of the new vehicle uses a hitherto-familiar media-communicating device, including utopian 3D posters that have not yet been used by a car brand in Italy.
The billboard action, which consists of three phases, will dominate the central shopping street Corso Como of Milan until November 15.
The first stage of this new type of media communication will begin with a three-dimensional presentation of the car, in the framework of which the new SUV will be displayed with the help of special spectacles distributated around the Corso Como, in an almost real-world scale and three-dimensional form.
The viewer of the picture will feel as if the car is emerging from the poster.
Subsequently, the innovative Elumina8 technology delivers every detail of the new GLK one by one to come together into a unified image.
Undoubtedly, with this promotion, Mercedes is trying to introduce something new into the stereotypical advertising world of the automotive industry.
Will you be able to arouse the interest of prospective buyers? We’ll see.
